enses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1818,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/pulls/26681","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/26681","diff_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/26681.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/pull/26681.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-01T18:37:53Z"},"body":"Users can't easily update the certificates in the embedded JDK and arguably shouldn't even have to be aware of the fact that Bazel relies on a bundled JVM. Since JDK 23 made it possible to rely on the system store on all major OSes, do so by default.\n\nRELNOTES[INC]: Bazel releases that include a bundled JDK now use the system trust store for certificates by default. Set `-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore` and `-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStoreType` via `--host_jvm_args` to override the default location.\n\nFixes #16223\nFixes #10349\n\nCloses #26664.\n\nPiperOrigin-RevId: 789262277\nChange-Id: Iab581bdfcb2971452e96f707006fc00a5a3228ec\n\nCommit https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/commit/1e50d2bb74dbe304777564353640972d2cf6bc52","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/26681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/26681/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":18945017378,"node_id":"REFE_lADOATz7jc5RN4vSzwAAAARpNgYi","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/18945017378","actor":{"login":"github-merge-queue[bot]","id":11834467